    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d737">

                <pb facs="0852" n="1686" xml:id="pg1686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1066</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-28T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 28, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 29, 2 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1484. Department’s 1222, June 13, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d737-f1"/>
                    Alfred G. Smith, accompanied by Capt. W. H.
                        Ellis, arrived Madrid, this morning.</p>
                <p>British Embassy, under date of 22d instant, informed this Embassy as follows:
                        “Carlton Levick of the Ministry of Shipping is leaving
                    for Madrid today in order to act as adviser on behalf of His Majesty’s
                    Government in these negotiations and he is further directed to act as adviser to
                    His Majesty’s Embassy in the same manner as Smith to
                    yourself.” Levick has arrived in Madrid. Negotiations,
                    under article 13, Spanish-American agreement, March 7, 1918, will be initiated
                    so soon as Chadbourne
                    who has been ill past week has recovered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
